<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jugurthine War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">112–105 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bellum-iugurthinum">The Jugurthine War</a> was fought from 112 to 105 BCE between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a>, king of Numidia. It began after Jugurtha seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cirta">Cirta</a> and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adherbal">Adherbal</a> and the Italian traders there, and Roman efforts were long hampered by bribery and defeats. Quintus Caecilius Metellus and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-marius">Gaius Marius</a> gained the upper hand, and Jugurtha was finally betrayed to Marius's quaestor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a> by King Bocchus of Mauretania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jugurthine-war.jpg" alt="Jugurthine War" width="320" height="144" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sulla_Coin2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
